  "case": "Owner case 05.10.2026 (live defect on MAIN-PC): on ellego.fi/contact the person cards (name, title, phone) are visible on the very first contact page, yet the collector walked between the page's sections in a circle and extracted nobody. The fixture reproduces two probable mechanisms. (a) A WordPress-like mega menu rendered open in the header of every page: more than 9000 characters of visible menu text (product categories, product names, services, industries, references and news, English and Finnish words, all invented) come before the first person card in document.body.innerText, so a page text clipped to its first few thousand characters holds no person at all. (b) 40 people under six h2 group headings (Sales & Marketing 8, Service 8, Spare parts 6, Project management 6, Logistics 6, Finance & Administration 6); every card has name, English title and phone, every second card also an email, so one model reply listing all of them is long. Above the cards a filter bar of plain buttons (no role=tab, no aria-selected, no aria-expanded): All, active on load and marked by a class only, and one button per group; a group button hides the other groups (hidden attribute), All shows them again. Every group is visible on load, so every card can be read without any click, and a model can click the filters in a circle. Expected: the collector reads every card on contact/ before any navigation or click and stops clicking the same filters; the five owner-named Sales & Marketing people (priority) come first. The other pages (/, products/, services/, references/, company/) carry the same header, mega menu and footer and no people; the footer holds the organization channel (switchboard and general email).",
